# Mobile App Typography

**CRITICAL:** Do NOT hardcode font sizes. Use CSS variables or typography utility classes.

## Text Sizes (use `var(--app-font-size-*)`)

- `--app-font-size-caption` (0.75rem) – pills, badges, metadata
- `--app-font-size-body-sm` (0.875rem) – secondary text, labels
- `--app-font-size-body` (1rem) – default body
- `--app-font-size-title` (1.0625rem) – card/list titles
- `--app-font-size-display` (1.25rem) – page titles
- `--app-font-size-display-lg` (1.5rem) – hero, big numbers

## Icon Sizes (use `var(--app-icon-size-*)`)

- `--app-icon-size-sm` through `--app-icon-size-4xl`
- `--app-icon-size-header`, `--app-icon-size-tab`, `--app-icon-size-fab`

## Typography Classes (prefer these)

- `.app-title`, `.app-body`, `.app-body-secondary`, `.app-body-sm`, `.app-body-secondary-sm`
- `.app-caption`, `.app-display`, `.app-display-lg`, `.app-link`

## Rules

1. **Never** use `font-size`, `font-weight`, `color`, or `line-height` for text in component SCSS. Use typography classes in HTML instead.
2. **Never** use `font-size: Xrem` or `font-size: Xpx` in component styles. Use vars only when a class cannot apply (e.g. icon sizing).
3. **Never** add new font-size variables without updating `docs/TYPOGRAPHY-GUIDE.md`.
4. Use **weight and color** for hierarchy, not more size steps.
5. **Before adding text styles** to any component: check if `.app-title`, `.app-body`, `.app-body-secondary`, `.app-body-secondary-sm`, `.app-caption`, `.app-display`, `.app-display-lg`, or semantic HTML (h1–h6, p) already provides the style.

## Anti-Pattern (causes redundant styles)

```scss
// ❌ BAD – component-level text styles
.my-component-title {
  font-size: var(--app-font-size-display);
  font-weight: var(--app-font-weight-semibold);
  color: var(--app-text-primary);
}
```

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD – use typography class in HTML -->
<h2 class="app-display">Title</h2>
```

